  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Layout",
      "items": [
        "Both halves have the same shape: a model class (RNNModel, SRModel), the step that produces it, and loading",
        "SR uses fitting.py instead of training.py: sigma_v is a one-pass estimate, not gradient training",
        "Steps that combine both halves sit at model/: training.py (Step 3) and prediction.py (Step 4)",
        "Saved files are drawn with the half that writes and reads them; they live under models/, not in the package"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Training (Step 3)",
      "items": [
        "Frames are loaded once; the SR model gets raw positions, the GRU their Eq. 1 local mean components",
        "SR is fitted, not trained: sigma_v per cell is a one-pass estimate with no loss or epochs",
        "SR is fitted and saved even when stochastic.enabled is off, so the saved pair is complete"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Prediction (Step 4)",
      "items": [
        "x = x_bar_RNN + v_tilde * dt_step, with v_tilde ~ N(0, sigma_v(x)^2) at each particle's current cell",
        "The pipeline passes a just-trained GRU in memory (skipping load_rnn) but never the SR model",
        "Autoregressive feeds predictions back; teacher-forced (default) reads the next frame from data_dir"
      ]
    }
  ]
